# Packages installed outside of install/packages.sh or optional packages
# Utilized by ISO builder to ensure package availability in the ISO
#
# Upstream's copy of this file is a hardware-driver catalogue: nvidia, vulkan,
# intel media, T2 MacBook, Surface, Dell XPS, Framework, limine and the dkms
# stack behind them. None of it applies to a GPU-less machine, and almost all
# of it is AUR or x86_64-only. broadcom-wl is the one entry with real bearing
# on a MacBook, and install/hardware/fix-bcm43xx.sh already installs it on
# demand for the chips it matches. The per-package reasoning, with the
# availability check behind it, is in docs/RELEASE-NOTES.md under "Package
# divergence from upstream".

base-devel
gst-plugin-pipewire
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
wireless-regdb

# A1181 MacBook support packages. Neither is in the archlinux32 repos (both
# are AUR upstream); they are self-built for the fork package repo, and
# install/hardware/apple/fix-a1181.sh skips them gracefully while absent.
mbpfan
isight-firmware-tools
